---

<section class="bg-white py-12 lg:py-24 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Methodology</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600">
        The analytical process is designed for one purpose: producing a technical conclusion that can be defended — in front of an investment committee, a lender, or a counterparty. It does not validate for the sake of completion.
        <br/><br/>
        <strong>It produces documented conclusions with explicit confidence.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="relative border-l-2 border-slate-200 ml-4 lg:ml-8 space-y-16">
      <div class="relative pl-8 lg:pl-12">
        <div class="absolute -left-[9px] top-2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-slate-900 ring-4 ring-white"></div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">1. Evidence Ingestion & Classification</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl">
          All available materials — regulatory filings, technical disclosures, contracts, permits, or project documentation — are ingested and classified by source authority, reliability, and relevance to the mandate. Nothing is assumed to be complete. Everything is tagged.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative pl-8 lg:pl-12">
        <div class="absolute -left-[9px] top-2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-slate-400 ring-4 ring-white"></div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">2. Multi-Dimensional Risk Analysis</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mb-4">
          Each technical dimension is scored independently: regulatory and permitting exposure, commercial structure, operational resilience, delivery execution, safety architecture, and technology fit. Findings are weighted by their materiality to the specific mandate.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mb-4">
          Evidence gaps are formally registered — never silently absorbed into the analysis.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-600 mb-6">
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-slate-900">
               <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-green-500 rounded-full"></span> Verified:
            </div>
            <p class="pl-4 text-slate-500">Confirmed by independent tangible evidence (e.g., stamped engineering drawings, published interconnection study results).</p>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-slate-900">
               <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span> Assumed:
            </div>
            <p class="pl-4 text-slate-500">Based on industry standard practice but unverified by project-specific documentation. Flagged explicitly as risk.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-red-600">
               <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-red-500 rounded-full"></span> Critical Silence:
            </div>
            <p class="pl-4 text-slate-500">Material omissions that undermine technical confidence, execution viability, or insurance positioning.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="relative pl-8 lg:pl-12">
        <div class="absolute -left-[9px] top-2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-slate-400 ring-4 ring-white"></div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">3. Documented Technical Conclusion</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mb-4">
          The output is a formal technical conclusion with a traceable decision rationale — not a narrative summary. Every conclusion is tied to evidence. Every confidence level is stated explicitly. Every outstanding item is logged.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 border-l-4 border-slate-900 p-4">
             <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Technical conclusions that hold up under scrutiny.</p>
             <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
                Because every finding can be traced back to the evidence it came from — in front of an IC, a credit committee, or a counterparty.
             </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
